        exam: [.direct("What did you see behind the laundromat?", "\"{V} was knifed twice after an argument over a parking space. I saw {D} run off right afterward.\""), .direct("What do the phone clips show?", "\"{DL} in a distinctive shirt holding a knife. Several people filmed it and walked on without calling anyone.\""), .direct("What did the surgical report show?", "\"Two deep stab wounds. {V} needed surgery.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your job at the laundromat.", "\"I work the counter at the laundromat. I make change, help customers with machines, and I watch the lot because arguments over parking happen a lot there.\""), .direct("What did you see happen around noon?", "\"I heard {DL} and {V} arguing over a parking space. Later I saw {DL} run off from behind the building, and I called for help.\""), .direct("What did you find when you went behind the laundromat?", "\"{V} was on the ground with two deep stab wounds. I pressed a towel on the wounds until paramedics arrived, and {V} was taken to the hospital.\""), .cross("{D} says {V} came at {D.him} with a pipe, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A pipe was on the ground afterward. {V}'s prints are on it, I understand.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} swing the pipe?", "\"No. I saw the aftermath. I did not see a swing.\""), .cross("Had the defendant argued with {V} earlier?", "\"Yes. {DL} had cursed at {V} earlier that day.\""), .cross("Did you see the stabbing itself?", "\"No. I saw {DL} run off afterward. I did not see who started what happened, and I cannot say who first had a weapon.\""), .cross("Did you see a pipe near the dumpster?", "\"I heard that a pipe was found there afterward. I did not see anyone holding it, and I cannot say whose it was.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Customer",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did you see a pipe in the lot after the stabbing?", "\"On the ground after. It lay near where {V} fell, and I noticed it when I walked over.\""), .direct("Who dropped the pipe in the lot, as far as you know?", "\"I do not know. I did not see anyone drop it. I only saw it lying there.\""), .direct("Where were you when this happened behind the laundromat?", "\"In the lot, near my car. I saw the end of the fight and the people filming.\""), .direct("Walk us through what you were doing at the laundromat that day.", "\"I was washing clothes and carrying baskets in and out. I was in the lot when I heard shouting from behind the building, and I looked over.\""), .direct("What did you see on the ground after the stabbing?", "\"A steel pipe lay near the dumpster, close to where {V} fell. I did not see anyone pick it up, and I did not touch it.\""), .direct("What did you notice about how {D} and {V} acted?", "\"Both were angry. I could hear them shouting, but I could not make out the words. I did not see anyone throw a punch.\""), .cross("Did you call anyone after what you saw?", "\"No. I did not. Many of us stood there. I am ashamed of that.\""), .cross("Did you see {V} holding the pipe?", "\"No. I did not see that. I only saw it on the ground afterward, so I cannot say who had it or when.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant stab {V}?", "\"No. I did not see the stabbing. I saw {D} walking fast away from the building and heard people shouting that someone was hurt.\""), .cross("You did not see who brought the pipe to the confrontation, did you?", "\"No. I saw the pipe on the ground after the fight. I did not see who held it first or who dropped it.\""), .cross("You did not see the stabbing itself, did you?", "\"No. I was inside the laundromat and came out when I heard shouting. By then it was over.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} knifed a stranger over a space.", "Self-defense."),
        allocution: "\"I panicked and ran.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} had cursed at {V} earlier that day.", "{V}'s prints are on the pipe."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you stab {V}?", "\"Yes. {V} came at me with a pipe after an argument over a parking space, and I used a knife.\""), .direct("Why did you run?", "\"I was terrified. I did not know what I had done. I ran, and I should have stayed.\""), .direct("What about the shirt in the clips?", "\"It is my shirt. I wore it that day. I know it is recognizable.\""), .direct("Tell the jury what led up to the confrontation.", "\"We argued over a parking space around noon. I was angry and I cursed at {V}. I did not think it would turn into anything more.\""), .direct("What happened behind the laundromat?", "\"{V} came at me with a steel pipe. I was terrified and I pulled out a knife. I stabbed {V} twice because I thought I was about to be hit.\""), .direct("What did you do afterward?", "\"I ran. I was frightened and I did not know what to do. I threw the knife away, and I turned myself in the next day.\""), .cross("{V} suffered two deep stab wounds. Was that necessary?", "\"I did not count. I was afraid. I know it was more than it needed to be.\""), .cross("{V}'s prints are on the pipe. Does that prove {V} attacked you?", "\"It shows {V} held it. I believe {V} came at me with it.\""), .cross("You had cursed at {V} earlier that day, hadn't you?", "\"Yes. We argued over the space, and I said things I should not have said. I know that does not look good.\""), .cross("You carried a knife with you, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I carry one for work and for my own safety. I did not go looking for a fight, and I never planned to use it.\""), .cross("You ran away instead of calling for help, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I panicked and ran. I should have called for help, and I live with the thought that I did not.\"")],
        openings: ("{V} was knifed twice behind a laundromat after an argument over a parking space. Several people filmed on their phones and walked on, and {D} was identified from a distinctive shirt in the clips.", "By the end of this trial, the proof will show that {V} came at {D} with a pipe, that {V}'s prints are on it, and that {D} acted in fear."),
        closings: ("Two stab wounds, a shirt in the phone clips, a clerk who saw {D} run, and a parking argument that ended in a knife. {D} fled the scene.", "A pipe with {V}'s prints on it and a person who used a knife in fear. The State must prove {D} was not defending {D.himself}."),
        timeline: [(0, "Noon: the parking argument."), (0, "12:20 p.m.: behind the laundromat."), (0, "12:25 p.m.: the stabbing."), (1, "Identified from video.")],
        identified: "Phone clips.",
        aggravating: ["The offense involved a weapon"],
        mood: .divided,
        impact: "Seven people walked past me.",
        doctrines: ["selfDefense", "imperfectSelfDefense"],
        genders: ["V": .male])

    static let unneededSurgeriesV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.unneededSurgeries",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Knee Specialist Billed for Replacements Healthy Joints Never Needed", "Imaging Reviews Showed Little Wear"],
        law: "insuranceFraud",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Presented false claims to an insurer, {V}, totaling $185,000, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 32...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, an orthopedic surgeon, billed $185,000 on {DATE} for knee operations that outside doctors say were not needed. A billing complaint from a patient started the review. {DL} says each patient had pain.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Billing Records", "Nine knee operations billed in one season."), E(.forensic, 3, "Outside Imaging Reviews", "Joints looked healthy."), E(.statement, 2, "Patient Complaint", "A patient was told surgery was the only choice.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Pain Notes", "{DL} points to charted pain.")],
        role: "Insurer physician reviewer",
        exam: [.direct("What did you review in {D}'s billing?", "\"Nine knee operations billed in one season for $185,000. A patient's billing complaint started my review.\""), .direct("What did outside doctors find?", "\"The joints looked healthy on imaging. No surgical need was found in the outside reviews.\""), .direct("What did the patient say?", "\"That the patient was told surgery was the only choice. The patient had not tried less invasive options.\""), .direct("Describe your job as a physician reviewer for the jury.", "\"I review claims for an insurer. I am an orthopedic doctor myself, so I review the medical records and imaging behind surgeries that look unusual.\""), .direct("How did the review of the defendant's cases begin?", "\"A patient filed a billing complaint after being told surgery was the only choice. That led us to look at nine knee operations billed in one season.\""), .direct("What did the imaging show?", "\"Outside doctors reviewed the images and found the joints looked healthy. In many of those cases, there was no sign of damage that would require surgery.\""), .cross("{D} says each patient had pain, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A physical therapist says patients did hurt. I agree with that.\""), .cross("Did some patients improve afterward?", "\"Two patients later improved. That is accurate.\""), .cross("Does a surgeon's pay rise with each surgery?", "\"Yes. {D}'s pay rose with each one.\""), .cross("Did the patients report pain?", "\"Yes. The charts record pain. Pain is real, but it does not always mean surgery is needed, and other treatments should usually come first.\""), .cross("Did any patients improve after surgery?", "\"Two patients later improved. I cannot say whether the surgery or something else helped, and I do not review how every patient did afterward.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Physical therapist",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D}'s patients hurt before the operations?", "\"Yes. They came to me in pain, with swelling and trouble walking. They were not faking it.\""), .direct("Were less invasive options tried first?", "\"Not all. Some patients tried therapy, and others went straight to surgery.\""), .direct("How did patients do after their surgeries?", "\"Some improved, and some did not. Two improved a lot, from what I saw.\""), .direct("Please explain your role as a physical therapist.", "\"I treat patients before and after orthopedic surgery. I work with surgeons and I see how patients move, how much pain they report, and how they heal.\""), .direct("What did you see about the defendant's patients before surgery?", "\"They came in with real pain. They had swelling and limited movement, and many could not walk without help. I saw it myself at the clinic.\""), .direct("How did the patients do afterward?", "\"Some improved and some did not. That is normal after knee surgery. Two patients I treated were walking much better a few months afterward.\""), .cross("Would you have recommended surgery for each of those nine patients?", "\"Not all. I would have tried more therapy first for several.\""), .cross("Did the imaging match the patients' pain?", "\"Not always. Some imaging looked healthy, which is confusing.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant tell a patient that surgery was the only choice?", "\"I did not hear that. I only heard it afterward.\""), .cross("Did every patient try therapy before surgery?", "\"No. Some tried therapy, and others went straight to the operating room. I cannot say that every patient had exhausted other options.\""), .cross("Can you say whether each surgery was necessary?", "\"No. I am not the surgeon, and I did not review the imaging. I can only describe the pain patients reported and how they did later.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} billed for needless operations.", "Treating real pain."),
        allocution: "\"I pushed too hard.\"",
        truths: ("{DL}'s pay rose with each surgery.", "Two patients later improved."),
        defendant: [.direct("Were those knee operations necessary?", "\"I believed so. Each patient had pain, and I judged that surgery would help. I made my best call each time.\""), .direct("Why did you not try less invasive options first?", "\"In some cases I did. In others the pain was severe, and I thought surgery was the better path.\""), .direct("Does your pay rise with each surgery?", "\"Yes. I am paid per procedure. I did not operate for that reason.\""), .direct("Tell us about your practice.", "\"I have been an orthopedic surgeon for many years. I see patients with knee pain every week, and I recommend surgery only when I believe it is needed.\""), .direct("How did you decide to operate on these nine patients?", "\"Each patient came to me in pain with swelling or limited movement. I examined them and reviewed their histories, and I believed surgery would help.\""), .direct("What do you say about the outside imaging reviews?", "\"Imaging does not show everything. A joint can look healthy on a scan and still cause pain. I treat the patient, not just the picture.\""), .cross("Nine operations, $185,000, and outside doctors say none were needed. How is that judgment?", "\"Doctors differ. I made calls I believed in.\""), .cross("A patient was told surgery was the only choice. Is that true?", "\"I explained the options. The patient chose surgery. I did not say it was the only one.\""), .cross("Your pay rises with each operation. Isn't that a conflict?", "\"It is. I know it looks that way. I tried to put patients first.\""), .cross("You are paid for each procedure, aren't you?", "\"Yes. I am paid per procedure. I know that creates a pressure, but it did not decide which patients I operated on.\""), .cross("You did not try less invasive options with every patient, did you?", "\"Not with every patient. In some cases, the pain was severe and I believed surgery was the better path. I stand by that judgment.\"")],
        openings: ("{D}, an orthopedic surgeon, billed $185,000 for nine knee operations in one season that outside doctors say were not needed, after a patient's billing complaint. {D}'s pay rose with each surgery.", "The defense will present evidence that each patient had real pain, that surgeons honestly differ on when to operate, and that two patients improved after surgery."),
        closings: ("Nine knee operations, healthy joints on outside imaging, a patient told surgery was the only choice, and pay that rose with each one. Patients were operated on without need.", "A surgeon who judged that patients in pain needed surgery and two who improved. The State must prove {D} knew the surgeries were unnecessary."),
        timeline: [(-240, "The season of surgeries begins."), (0, "The patient complaint."), (30, "Outside reviews."), (90, "Charges.")],
        identified: "A patient complaint.",
        aggravating: ["The defendant took advantage of a position of trust or confidence", "The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I still limp.",
        doctrines: ["expertTestimony"])

    static let phantomPatientClaimsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.phantomPatientClaims",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Transport Firm Billed for Rides to Dialysis That Never Took Place", "Dead Patients Among Riders Claimed"],
        law: "insuranceFraud",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Presented false claims to an insurer, {V}, totaling $390,000, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 28...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} ran a medical transport firm that billed $390,000 by {DATE} for rides to dialysis for dozens of riders, some of whom had died. Trip sheets were signed in matching ink. {DL} says drivers filled in sheets late and sloppily.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Trip Sheets", "Rides billed for riders who had died."), E(.digital, 3, "Fleet GPS", "Vans parked on days of billed trips."), E(.document, 2, "Insurer Payments", "$390,000 paid to {D}'s firm.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Late Paperwork", "{DL} says drivers filled sheets in late.")],
        role: "Insurer fraud analyst",
        exam: [.direct("What do the trip sheets show?", "\"Rides billed for riders who had died, with signatures in matching ink. They look signed by one hand.\""), .direct("Tell us about your work as an insurer fraud analyst.", "\"I review billing for health insurers and look for patterns that suggest fraud. I use payment records, GPS data, and trip sheets to test what was billed.\""), .direct("What did you find in {D}'s billing?", "\"The firm billed $390,000 for rides to dialysis for dozens of riders. Some of the riders had died before the dates of billed trips.\""), .direct("What did the fleet GPS show?", "\"On billed days, vans were parked and had not moved. The GPS data does not support many of the trips that were billed.\""), .direct("How did you compare the trip sheets to the insurer's records?", "\"I matched each billed ride to a rider's status, then to GPS data. Several rides were billed after the rider had died.\""), .direct("What patterns did you notice in the signatures on the trip sheets?", "\"Many sheets were signed in the same pen with the same slant, even on different days and by different named drivers.\""), .cross("{D} says drivers filled in sheets late and sloppily, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. Many billed trips did happen and were logged, and That is fair.\""), .cross("Did real trips run?", "\"Many did. I do not dispute that.\""), .cross("Who signed the sheets?", "\"{D} signed many of them.\""), .cross("Did some billed trips actually take place?", "\"Yes. Many trips happened and were logged. My concern is with the trips that were billed for riders who had died.\""), .cross("Could drivers have filled sheets late and sloppily?", "\"That is possible, and I have seen sloppy paperwork. But sloppiness does not explain billing for people who were no longer alive.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Dispatcher",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did real trips run that were billed?", "\"Many. We ran real trips to dialysis every day, and many billed trips did happen and were logged.\""), .direct("Who signed the trip sheets for the riders?", "\"{D}, often. {D.He} signed sheets when drivers were late or forgot to have riders sign.\""), .direct("Did drivers fill sheets in sloppily or late?", "\"Yes. Drivers filled in sheets at the end of the day, sometimes the next day, and mistakes crept in.\""), .direct("Tell us about your job as a dispatcher.", "\"I dispatch vans for the transport firm. I assign riders to drivers, track the schedule, and answer calls from patients who need a ride.\""), .direct("How many real trips did the firm run each day?", "\"Dozens, to dialysis and other appointments. I scheduled them myself. Many riders were regulars, and I knew their names and their schedules well.\""), .direct("How were trip sheets handled by drivers?", "\"Drivers filled them in late, often at the end of the day. Some forgot, and {D.he} would sign the sheets to catch up on the paperwork.\""), .cross("Did you see {D} sign sheets for riders who had died?", "\"No. I did not see that. I only saw {DF} sign sheets in general.\""), .cross("Were vans parked on days when trips were billed?", "\"Some days, yes. I do not know why.\""), .cross("Do you keep the logs for each trip in your dispatch?", "\"Yes. I keep logs, but not for every trip. Some were missed.\""), .cross("Did you know that some riders had died?", "\"Sometimes I heard about it late. We did not always get a call, and a name could stay on the schedule for a while.\""), .cross("Did you review the billing sent to insurers?", "\"No. I only handled dispatch. I never reviewed what was billed, and I cannot say what dates or names were on the claims.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} billed for rides no one took.", "Sloppy paperwork."),
        allocution: "\"I let the billing run wild.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} signed the sheets for dead riders.", "Many billed trips did happen and were logged."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you bill for rides to dead riders?", "\"No. I did not knowingly bill for anyone who had died. Drivers filled in sheets late and sloppily.\""), .direct("Who signed the trip sheets?", "\"I signed many myself. I signed when drivers forgot to get riders' signatures. I should not have.\""), .direct("Did the billed trips happen?", "\"Many did. We ran real trips every day. Some of the sheets were wrong, and I did not check them.\""), .direct("What can you tell us about your transport company?", "\"I run a medical transport company. We take dialysis patients to treatment several times a week, and many of our riders depend on us.\""), .direct("How did the trip sheets get filled out?", "\"Drivers wrote them, and sometimes late. When drivers forgot, I signed sheets myself to keep the paperwork moving. It was sloppy, and I know that.\""), .direct("What happened when the insurer questioned the billing?", "\"I told them our paperwork was sloppy and that many trips were real. I did not knowingly bill for anyone who had died.\""), .cross("Riders who had died were billed for rides, weren't they?", "\"Yes. The sheets were wrong. I did not catch it.\""), .cross("Vans were parked on days of billed trips. How do you explain that?", "\"I cannot. Some sheets were filled in wrong.\""), .cross("$390,000 was paid to your firm. Will you repay what was wrong?", "\"Yes. I will repay whatever the insurer finds was not owed.\""), .cross("You signed sheets for riders who had died, didn't you?", "\"Yes, I signed many sheets late. I did not check each name, and I did not realize some riders had died. I should have, yes.\""), .cross("Vans were parked on days of billed trips, weren't they?", "\"On some days, yes. Not every billed trip was driven that day, and the records were not kept the way they should have been.\"")],
        openings: ("{D} ran a medical transport firm that billed $390,000 for dialysis rides, including rides for riders who had died. Trip sheets were signed in matching ink, and the fleet GPS shows vans parked on billed days.", "The defense witnesses will explain that many billed trips did happen and were logged, and that sloppy paperwork by drivers is a mistake and not a fraud."),
        closings: ("$390,000 in rides billed for riders who had died, vans parked on billed days, and sheets signed in matching ink. This was a ghost billing scheme.", "A busy transport firm with real trips and sloppy paperwork. The State must prove {D} knowingly billed for rides that never happened."),
        timeline: [(-220, "Billing begins."), (0, "Year 1: the audit."), (0, "Year 1: the GPS pull."), (30, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Fleet GPS and trip sheets.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let tornadoReliefKeptV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.tornadoReliefKept",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Flood Relief Fund Pocketed Most of $120,000 Raised for Families", "Collection Jars and a New Boat"],
        law: "falsePretenses100k",
        threshold: 8,
        spec: "Obtained over $100,000 by false pretenses from {V} and other donors, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 30...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "After a river flood, {D} ran an online and storefront drive and raised $120,000 by {DATE}. Only $11,000 reached families. The rest went to {D}'s mortgage and a boat. {DL} says costs and storage ate the money.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Fund Page", "'Every cent will reach flood families.'"), E(.document, 3, "Bank Statements", "$11,000 to families; the rest to {D}."), E(.statement, 2, "Church Pantry", "Few deliveries ever arrived.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Storage Costs", "{DL} says storage and fuel were real costs.")],
        role: "Donor",
        exam: [.direct("What did you give to {D}'s flood relief drive?", "\"A donation to a fund whose page said, 'Every cent will reach flood families.' I gave because of that promise.\""), .direct("What do the bank statements show?", "\"$11,000 reached families out of $120,000 raised. The rest went to {D}'s mortgage and a boat.\""), .direct("What did a church pantry tell you?", "\"Few deliveries ever arrived. The pantry says almost nothing came.\""), .direct("Tell us why you gave to the flood relief drive.", "\"The river flood destroyed homes in my region. I wanted to help families rebuild, and I trusted a drive that promised every cent would reach them.\""), .direct("How much did you give and how did you give it?", "\"I gave through the fund page online. The page said, Every cent will reach flood families, and that promise was why I gave.\""), .direct("What did you learn afterward about where the money went?", "\"Bank statements showed $11,000 reached families out of $120,000 raised. The rest went to {D.him}, including a mortgage and a boat loan.\""), .cross("{D} says costs and storage ate the money, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"Yes. A storage unit manager says {DL} rented a unit and bought supplies. I will agree that may be true.\""), .cross("Did {D} deliver some supplies?", "\"Some, yes. Not much.\""), .cross("Did the defendant pay a boat loan with the fund?", "\"Yes. A boat loan was paid from the fund.\""), .cross("Did the defendant tell donors about storage and fuel costs?", "\"Not on the page I saw. The page said every cent, and I never saw a notice about costs or about fees taken out.\""), .cross("Did you hear from families who received help?", "\"A church pantry told me few deliveries ever arrived. I did not speak to the families directly, only to the pantry.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Storage unit manager",
        defenseExam: [.direct("Did {D} rent a storage unit from you?", "\"For supplies. {D} rented a small unit and kept boxes there for the flood drive.\""), .direct("How big was the unit that the defendant rented?", "\"Small. A ten-by-ten unit, and it was not full. I saw it a few times.\""), .direct("Please tell us about your storage business.", "\"I manage a storage facility. I rent units by size and month, and I keep a record of who rents each unit and what they say they are storing.\""), .direct("What did the defendant rent from you?", "\"A small ten-by-ten unit, for supplies. {D.He} rented it for several months after the flood and paid by the month.\""), .direct("What did you see in the unit?", "\"Boxes of supplies, like water and blankets. The unit was not full, and I never saw anything that looked like a large amount of donated goods.\""), .direct("How long did the defendant keep the storage unit rented?", "\"About five months. {D.He} paid rent in cash at first and then stopped. I opened the unit when the rent was past due and found boxes of old clothing.\""), .cross("Did you see supplies leave the unit for flood families?", "\"Some. I saw {DF} load a truck once. I do not know where it went.\""), .cross("Did the defendant pay rent on time?", "\"Yes. {D.He} paid on time. I have no complaint about that.\""), .cross("Would a small unit take $120,000 worth of supplies?", "\"No. It could not hold that much. It was small.\""), .cross("How full was the unit during the time {D} rented it?", "\"Not very. I saw it on a few visits. Some boxes were stacked, but there was plenty of space, and I cannot say what came and went.\""), .cross("Did you see the defendant deliver supplies to families?", "\"No. I never saw deliveries. I only saw {DF} come and go with the unit, and I cannot say what happened to the supplies.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} diverted flood donations.", "Real costs."),
        allocution: "\"I should have kept it separate.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} paid a boat loan from the fund.", "{DL} did rent a unit and bought supplies."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you keep the flood relief money?", "\"No. Costs and storage ate much of it. I rented a unit and bought supplies for families.\""), .direct("Why did only $11,000 reach families?", "\"Costs were high, and I did not have a system. I know that is not what I promised.\""), .direct("Tell the jury how the relief drive started.", "\"The river flooded our region, and I wanted to help. I set up an online page and a storefront collection, and donations came in fast.\""), .direct("What costs did you have running the drive?", "\"I rented a storage unit, bought supplies, and paid for fuel to haul water and blankets. Those costs were real, and I kept some receipts.\""), .direct("What do you say about the mortgage and the boat loan?", "\"I paid the boat loan and part of my mortgage from the fund. I told myself I would replace it, and I did not. I know that was wrong.\""), .direct("What did you promise donors when you opened the relief drive?", "\"That every cent would reach flood families. I believed it at the start, and I did not keep records the way I should have.\""), .cross("'Every cent will reach flood families.' Was that true?", "\"It was not true. I should not have written it.\""), .cross("$120,000 raised and only $11,000 delivered. Where did the rest go?", "\"To costs, to storage, and to my own bills. I used more than I should have, yes.\""), .cross("Will you repay the donors?", "\"I want to. I do not have the money now.\""), .cross("The page said every cent will reach flood families, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is what the page said. I should have been honest about costs from the beginning, and I did not change the page.\""), .cross("Only $11,000 of $120,000 reached families, didn't it?", "\"Yes. That is what the bank statements show. I wish I could say it was more, and I take responsibility for the rest.\"")],
        openings: ("After a river flood, {D} ran a relief drive that raised $120,000 under the promise 'Every cent will reach flood families.' Only $11,000 reached families, and the rest paid {D}'s mortgage and a boat.", "Listen for the defense evidence, which will show that {D} rented storage and bought supplies, that costs were real, and that {D} meant to help flood families."),
        closings: ("$120,000 raised, $11,000 delivered, a boat loan and a mortgage paid, and a promise that every cent would reach families. That promise was false.", "A relief drive with real costs and a real storage unit and a person who meant to help. The State must prove {D} meant to deceive the donors."),
        timeline: [(-40, "The flood."), (0, "The drive closes."), (50, "Families ask."), (110, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Bank statements.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain", "The victim was particularly vulnerable"],
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "We gave what little we had.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let slowCarHoodClaimsV1 = SmallCases.make(
