        state: [E(.video, 3, "Deck Cameras", "{D} steps behind a car that is already reversing."), E(.document, 3, "Claim Files", "Seven claims against different insurers."), E(.document, 2, "Attorney Letters", "The same law office each time.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Careless Drivers", "{DL} says drivers failed to look.")],
        role: "Claims adjuster",
        exam: [.direct("How did {D} come to your attention as an adjuster?", "\"Seven injury claims in eighteen months, each filed against a different insurer, each describing a backing car in a parking deck. The pattern is what made me pull the files.\""), .direct("What do the deck cameras show?", "\"It shows {D} stepping out and walking behind a car that is already reversing, with the brake lights lit and the backup lamps on. It repeats in several of the clips.\""), .direct("What did the claim files contain?", "\"Seven separate claims, each with a statement of bumps and bruises, medical bills, and a demand for a settlement. Each one landed with a different carrier.\""), .direct("What did you notice about the attorney letters?", "\"The same law office wrote the demand letters every time, in nearly identical language, which is unusual for seven unrelated accidents.\""), .direct("Which decks were involved?", "\"Different parking decks around town. Several had older cameras with narrow views, though the clips we obtained are still clear on the key moments.\""), .direct("How much money was at stake across the claims?", "\"Tens of thousands of dollars across the seven claims once treatment bills and the demanded amounts were added together.\""), .cross("Drivers do fail to look when they back up, don't they?", "\"They do, and that is a real danger in decks. Some of these drivers admitted they did not look, and I do not dispute that.\""), .cross("Were the injuries documented by medical staff?", "\"Yes. An urgent care aide recorded bruising each time. I am not claiming the bruises were invented.\""), .cross("Would a person walking through a deck sometimes end up behind a reversing car by accident?", "\"It can happen once. Seven times in eighteen months in different decks is what makes me doubt it.\""), .cross("Did any driver say the defendant deliberately stepped into the car?", "\"No driver said that to me. The conclusion comes from the camera angles and the timing, not from a confession.\""), .cross("Have you proven the defendant chose decks with weak cameras?", "\"I cannot prove a choice. I can say the clips from the weakest cameras are the ones that show the least.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Urgent care aide",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What did you see when {D} came to urgent care?", "\"Fresh bruising on a hip and an arm each time, with soreness that matched being bumped by a slow vehicle.\""), .direct("How many times did you treat the defendant?", "\"Several visits over about a year and a half. I am an aide, so I assisted the provider and recorded vitals and complaints.\""), .direct("How severe were the injuries?", "\"Not serious. Mostly bruising and sore muscles, nothing that needed imaging or surgery, and patients were sent home with instructions.\""), .direct("Did the defendant behave as if in pain?", "\"{D} winced when moving the sore areas and favored one side. It looked like genuine discomfort to me.\""), .direct("Did the defendant describe how each injury happened?", "\"Each time {DF} said a car backing out had bumped into {D.him} in a deck, and the bruise pattern fit that kind of low-speed bump.\""), .direct("Was the care recorded the same way each visit?", "\"Yes. We chart complaint, exam findings, and instructions the same way for everyone, and nothing in {D.his} charts stood out as unusual.\""), .cross("Could bruising like that come from something other than a car?", "\"Bruises can come from many things, and I cannot say which one caused these. I only charted what I saw.\""), .cross("Did the defendant mention a lawyer to you at any visit?", "\"Once, {D.he} said a lawyer was helping with the claim. I did not ask questions about it.\""), .cross("Did you see any of the parking deck incidents?", "\"No. I only saw patients after the fact, so I cannot say how any bump happened.\""), .cross("Are you aware that the same bruising pattern repeated seven times?", "\"I saw some of the visits, not all of them. Seven in a year and a half seems like a lot, I will admit.\""), .cross("Would you expect a person bumped by a slow car to seek urgent care each time?", "\"Many people do when they feel sore, so I did not think it odd at the time.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} walked into reversing cars on purpose.", "Careless drivers."),
        allocution: "\"I am sorry for all of it.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} picked decks with the weakest cameras.", "{DL} was treated for real bruising each time."),
        defendant: [.direct("What do you do that puts you in parking decks so often?", "\"I walk to work and to appointments, and the decks are the shortest route through downtown. I cut through them most days.\""), .direct("What happened the first time a car bumped you?", "\"A driver backed out without looking, and the bumper caught my hip. I fell against a pillar and left with a bruise the size of a plate.\""), .direct("Did you stage any of these incidents?", "\"No. I did not plan or stage a single one. I was bumped, I was sore, and I reported it as I would any injury.\""), .direct("Why did you go to urgent care each time?", "\"I was sore, and I did not want to wait for it to get worse. The bruising showed up within a day or two.\""), .direct("Why did you hire the same lawyer?", "\"The first lawyer was fast and kind, and I stayed with the same office for the later ones instead of searching again.\""), .direct("What are your feelings about the claims now?", "\"I know seven looks like a lot. I only know I was hit, I was hurt, and I filed for what I was owed.\""), .cross("The camera shows you stepping behind a car that is already reversing, doesn't it?", "\"It shows me walking through a deck. I did not look at every car, and drivers do not always signal.\""), .cross("Seven claims against seven insurers in eighteen months. How is that bad luck?", "\"I walk through decks daily, and drivers back up without looking. It is bad luck and a busy route.\""), .cross("You walked into decks with weak cameras, didn't you?", "\"I walked into the decks near my work. I did not study the cameras.\""), .cross("Your lawyer wrote nearly identical demand letters seven times, didn't the lawyer?", "\"The lawyer uses a form letter. I did not write those letters or pick the wording.\""), .cross("You have been paid on some of these claims, haven't you?", "\"I was paid on a few, for my medical bills and some pain. I did not get rich from it.\"")],
        openings: ("Seven times in eighteen months, {D} was bumped by a car backing out of a parking deck and filed an injury claim against a different insurer each time. The deck cameras show {D} stepping behind cars that were already in reverse.", "{D} walks through parking decks every day and was hit by drivers who did not look. Real bruises, real treatment, and a lawyer's form letters do not make a plot."),
        closings: ("Seven claims, seven insurers, one law office, and clips that show {D} walking behind cars that were already reversing. Bad luck does not repeat this neatly.", "Drivers back up without looking, and a person who walks decks daily gets hit. Bruises were documented every time, and the State has not shown a plan."),
        timeline: [(-540, "The first deck claim."), (0, "The seventh claim."), (0, "Cameras are matched."), (75, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Deck camera footage.",
        aggravating: ["The offense was committed for pecuniary gain"],
        mood: .divided,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male])

    static let localCelebrityTrackerV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.localCelebrityTracker",
        category: .violent,
        headlines: ["Admirer Tailed Radio Host Across the County and Posted Her Whereabouts", "Same Silver Sedan at Nine Appearances"],
        law: "stalking",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Willfully harassed {V} on more than one occasion without legitimate purpose, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 18...60,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D} followed {V}, a local radio host, to nine appearances and posted {V.his} whereabouts on {DATE}. {V} had blocked {D} on social media and sent a written notice. {DL} says {D.he} was only a supporter.",
        state: [E(.digital, 3, "Social Posts", "Nine posts naming where {V} would be."), E(.video, 3, "Parking Lot Cameras", "A silver sedan registered to {D} at each stop."), E(.document, 2, "Cease Notice", "A written demand to stop.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Supporter", "{DL} says {D.he} was cheering {V} on.")],
        role: "Station manager",
        exam: [.direct("What was {D}'s connection to your station's events?", "\"{D} followed {V}, our local radio host, to nine public appearances over several weeks and posted {V}'s whereabouts online before each one.\""), .direct("What do the posts say?", "\"Nine posts naming where {V} would be and when. Several were put up hours before the appearance, with directions.\""), .direct("What do the parking lot cameras show?", "\"A silver sedan registered to {DL} parked at each of the nine stops. The plate and the car match every time.\""), .direct("What did {V} do about it?", "\"{V} blocked {DL} on social media and then sent a written notice demanding that {DL} stop. That is in our file.\""), .direct("What was the effect on {V}?", "\"{V} changed routines, asked for escorts, and told me {V} no longer felt safe arriving alone at events.\""), .direct("Did the posting continue after the notice?", "\"Yes. Posts continued after the written demand, and {D.he} showed up at appearances after it arrived.\""), .cross("Were these appearances public events?", "\"Yes. They were open to the public, and anyone could buy a ticket or walk in.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever threaten {V}?", "\"No. There was no threat in any post or message I have seen.\""), .cross("Did the defendant buy tickets and attend openly?", "\"{D.He} bought tickets and sat in view. I will not say {D.he} hid.\""), .cross("Many fans follow hosts to events, don't they?", "\"Some do. Nine in a row after being blocked and warned is outside what I call fandom.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever approach {V} physically?", "\"Not that anyone reported. {DL} stayed in the crowd.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Fan club member",
        defenseExam: [.direct("How long has {D} been a member of the fan club?", "\"Several years. {D} comes to our meetings and has been a loyal supporter of {V}'s show.\""), .direct("Did the defendant attend appearances openly?", "\"Always. {D.He} bought a ticket every time and sat in plain sight with the rest of the audience.\""), .direct("Did the defendant post about the appearances online?", "\"Yes, in the open, under {D.his} own name. Many of us post where we are going.\""), .direct("How did the defendant get to the appearances?", "\"{D.He} drove, sometimes a long way. {D.He} once drove through the night to reach one.\""), .direct("How did the defendant behave toward {V}?", "\"Politely. {DF} clapped, said hello in the line like everyone else, and never made a scene.\""), .direct("Does the club discourage anything like following?", "\"We tell members to be respectful and to leave hosts alone after the show.\""), .cross("Was {V} warned by the fan club to stay away?", "\"Not by us. I did not know of a written notice until later.\""), .cross("Did you know {V} had blocked {D}?", "\"I heard about it afterward. I did not know at the time.\""), .cross("Would you drive through the night to see a host nine times?", "\"Probably not. {D.He} is more devoted than I am.\""), .cross("Did the defendant keep posting after the notice?", "\"I believe so. I did not follow every post.\""), .cross("Did any club member tell the defendant to stop?", "\"Not that I recall. We did not think it was a problem until deputies were involved.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} tracked a host from stop to stop.", "A supporter."),
        allocution: "\"I did not hear the word stop.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} drove through the night to reach one appearance.", "{DL} paid for every ticket and posted in the open."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you attend nine of {V}'s appearances?", "\"I admire {V}'s show. It is the only radio I listen to, and the appearances are the only chance to see {V} in person.\""), .direct("Why did you post where {V} would be?", "\"I wanted other fans to know and to come out. I thought of it as sharing news, not tracking anyone.\""), .direct("What did you think when you were blocked?", "\"I assumed I had clicked something by mistake. I did not understand it as a message to stay away.\""), .direct("Did you receive the written notice?", "\"I received it. I read it, and I felt embarrassed. I did not think I was bothering anyone, and I should have listened.\""), .direct("How did you travel to the appearances?", "\"I drove. A couple were long trips, and one I drove through the night to make.\""), .direct("What do you want {V} to know?", "\"I am sorry I frightened {V}. I only meant to be a supporter, and I see now how it looked.\""), .cross("You attended appearances after the notice, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I did, because I did not think the notice applied to public events. I was wrong.\""), .cross("You kept posting {V}'s location, didn't you?", "\"I did. I did not stop to think about how a stranger would read it.\""), .cross("A silver sedan registered to you was at nine stops, wasn't it?", "\"Yes. That is my car. I was at each of them.\""), .cross("You drove through the night to reach an appearance. Is that casual fandom?", "\"I realize how that sounds. I was excited, and I did not count the hours.\""), .cross("You never asked {V} whether {V} minded?", "\"No. I never asked. I assumed a public figure would not mind.\"")],
        openings: ("For weeks, {D} followed {V}, a local radio host, to nine public appearances and posted {V}'s whereabouts online each time, after being blocked and sent a written notice to stop. Cameras tied {D}'s silver sedan to every stop.", "Nine events, every ticket bought, every post made under {D}'s own name. {D} is a devoted fan, loud and open, who never threatened or approached anyone and did not grasp the line."),
        closings: ("A notice to stop, a block on social media, and nine more appearances with nine more posts. A fan who keeps going after being told no has stopped being a fan.", "{D} bought tickets, posted in the open, and never said a word of threat. Enthusiasm that crosses a line is not the same as stalking."),
        timeline: [(-75, "The first appearance."), (-10, "The notice."), (0, "The ninth appearance."), (28, "Charges.")],
        identified: "Parking lot cameras.",
        mood: .wantsConviction,
        impact: "I began varying my route home.",
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"],
        genders: ["D": .male, "V": .female])

    static let syrupReserveHeistV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.syrupReserveHeist",
        category: .property,
        headlines: ["Barrels of Co-op Syrup Roll Off a Loading Dock Under a Driver's Signature", "Tracker Tags Lead to a Restaurant Supplier"],
        law: "felonyLarceny",
        threshold: 6,
        spec: "Took and carried away property of {V} worth over $1,000, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 25...65,
        victim: true,
        summary: "{D}, a freight driver, signed out 60 barrels of maple syrup worth $150,000 from {V}'s co-op dock on {DATE} and delivered them to a restaurant supplier. Tracker tags on the barrels gave the route away. {DL} says a dock lead told {D.him} to haul them.",
        state: [E(.document, 3, "Bill of Lading", "Signed by {D}, with a blank customer line."), E(.digital, 3, "Tracker Tags", "Barrels ping at a supplier's warehouse."), E(.forensic, 2, "Barrel Lot Stamps", "The supplier's stock matches the co-op lots.")],
        defense: [E(.statement, 1, "Dock Lead", "{DL} says a dock lead gave a verbal go-ahead.")],
        role: "Co-op manager",
        exam: [.direct("What did {D} do at your co-op dock?", "\"{D}, a freight driver, signed out 60 barrels of maple syrup worth $150,000 and hauled them away on the date in question.\""), .direct("What does the bill of lading show?", "\"{DL}'s signature on the pickup, with the customer line left blank. Every other bill we have has a named customer.\""), .direct("How were the barrels found?", "\"Tracker tags on the barrels pinged from a restaurant supplier's warehouse, which gave away the route.\""), .direct("What did the lot stamps show?", "\"The supplier's stock carries lot stamps that match our co-op lots. They are our barrels, with no real question.\""), .direct("What was the loss to the co-op?", "\"$150,000 in syrup, plus the cost of weeks of investigation and a hole in our reserve for contract buyers.\""), .direct("Who is authorized to release barrels from the dock?", "\"Only a dock lead with a signed release order, which names the customer. None existed for this load.\""), .cross("{D} says a dock lead told {D.him} to haul the load, doesn't {D.he}?", "\"A dock lead did call {D.him} that morning, I understand. What the call said is the question.\""), .cross("Did {D} have a release order in hand?", "\"No. {D.He} signed the bill of lading without any release order that I can find.\""), .cross("Did anyone at the dock stop the truck?", "\"No. The barrels were loaded in the normal flow of the morning, and the gate released the truck.\""), .cross("Could a driver reasonably follow a lead's instruction?", "\"Drivers do follow leads. That is why the blank customer line bothers me more than the signature.\""), .cross("Did the defendant try to hide the route?", "\"No. {D.He} drove straight to the supplier. The trackers made that easy.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Dock worker",
        defenseExam: [.direct("What do you do at the co-op dock?", "\"I load and stage barrels on the dock under the leads' directions.\""), .direct("Did you see {D} on the day of the load?", "\"Yes. {D} backed in early and waited by the dock office.\""), .direct("Did a lead speak to the defendant?", "\"I overheard a chat between a lead and {DF} by the office. It was short, and the lead pointed at the barrel rows.\""), .direct("Was the chat about this load?", "\"I am not sure. Barrels were being staged for several trucks that morning.\""), .direct("How was the defendant treated by the leads?", "\"Friendly. {DF} is a regular driver, and the leads treat {DF} like family.\""), .direct("Do drivers usually ask questions about a load?", "\"Not much. If a lead says to load, they load, and paperwork follows.\""), .cross("Did you hear the lead say a customer name?", "\"No. I only caught part of it, and I did not hear a name.\""), .cross("Did you see a release order handed to the defendant?", "\"No. I did not see paper change hands.\""), .cross("Was it normal for the customer line to be blank?", "\"No. That is unusual. I noticed it only afterward.\""), .cross("Are you friends with the defendant?", "\"I know {D.him} from the dock. We are friendly, but I am telling you what I saw.\""), .cross("Did you load the barrels yourself?", "\"I loaded part of them. I did not check where they were going.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} signed out stock to sell.", "A verbal go-ahead."),
        allocution: "\"I should have waited for paper.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} took a cash payment from the supplier.", "A dock lead did call {DL} that morning."),
        defendant: [.direct("Did you steal the maple syrup?", "\"No. A dock lead called me that morning and told me to haul these barrels, so I picked them up and signed for them.\""), .direct("Why did you sign the bill of lading with the customer blank?", "\"The lead said the customer would be filled in. In a rush, I signed and trusted the paperwork would follow.\""), .direct("Where did you deliver the barrels?", "\"To a restaurant supplier I was told to use. I followed the address the lead gave me.\""), .direct("Did you know the barrels were not authorized?", "\"No. If I had known, I would not have touched them.\""), .direct("Why was the supplier paying you?", "\"The supplier paid cash for the haul and a small fee. I did not think it was strange.\""), .direct("What would you tell the co-op?", "\"I am sorry the load went wrong. I did what a driver does when a lead says go.\""), .cross("You took a cash payment from the supplier, didn't you?", "\"Yes. I was paid cash for the haul.\""), .cross("No release order was in your hand, was there?", "\"No. I did not ask for one.\""), .cross("Sixty barrels of syrup worth $150,000, and you never asked who the customer was?", "\"I trusted the lead. I should have asked.\""), .cross("Can the lead confirm the call?", "\"The lead did call me that morning. What the lead says about it is for the lead.\""), .cross("You drove the barrels straight to a supplier at half the value, didn't you?", "\"I delivered where I was told. I did not set any price.\"")],
        openings: ("Sixty barrels of maple syrup worth $150,000 left a co-op dock on a bill of lading signed by {D}, a freight driver, with the customer line blank. Tracker tags led straight to a restaurant supplier whose stock matches the co-op's lots.", "A dock lead called {D} that morning and told {D} to haul these barrels. A driver who follows a lead's call and signs the sheet put in front of {D} did not steal."),
        closings: ("A blank customer line, a cash payment from the supplier, and barrels that pinged all the way to the supplier's warehouse. {D} took the load and took the money.", "A dock lead's call, a signature on a rushed sheet, and a driver who did what drivers do. Nobody ever showed the release order, and nobody showed {D} knew."),
        timeline: [(-1, "A call to {DL}."), (0, "6 a.m.: barrels leave the dock."), (2, "The tags ping at the supplier."), (30, "The audit.")],
        identified: "Tracker tags.",
        mood: .indifferent,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let reptileHoardCrueltyV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.reptileHoardCruelty",
        category: .publicOrder,
        headlines: ["Rented Garage Full of Snakes and Lizards Found Cold and Dry", "Landlord's Odor Complaint Leads to Rescue"],
        law: "animalCruelty",
        threshold: 7,
        spec: "Intentionally and without justification failed to provide necessary sustenance and shelter to animals, on or about {DATE}.",
        ages: 22...65,
        victim: false,
        summary: "A landlord's complaint of a smell on {DATE} led officers to a rented garage where {D} kept about 70 snakes and lizards. Twenty-six were dead and the rest were dehydrated. {DL} says a power outage ruined the heat lamps.",
        state: [E(.forensic, 3, "Necropsy Findings", "Dehydration and chill."), E(.video, 3, "Officer Body Camera", "Dry bowls and unplugged lamps."), E(.document, 2, "Utility Records", "Power cut off for unpaid bills.")],
        defense: [E(.document, 1, "Outage Notice", "A utility outage notice.")],
        role: "Humane officer",
        exam: [.direct("What led you to the rented garage?", "\"A landlord complained of a smell on the date in question. We went to check and found about 70 snakes and lizards in the garage.\""), .direct("What condition were the animals in?", "\"Twenty-six were dead, and the rest were dehydrated and chilled. Several were barely moving when we opened the door.\""), .direct("What does your body camera show?", "\"Dry water bowls, unplugged heat lamps, and animals lying in cold enclosures. The garage was cold enough to see my breath.\""), .direct("What did the necropsy find?", "\"Dehydration and chill as the causes. These animals died of cold and thirst over a period of days.\""), .direct("What did the utility records show?", "\"Power to the garage had been cut off for unpaid bills. That explains the dead lamps but not the dry bowls.\""), .direct("What did you do with the surviving animals?", "\"We moved them to a rescue partner with heat and water, and a veterinarian began treating the dehydrated ones the same day.\""), .cross("A power outage can ruin heat lamps without any person's fault, can't it?", "\"It can ruin lamps, yes. Water is a separate matter, and it does not need power.\""), .cross("Did {D} cooperate when contacted?", "\"{D} answered when reached. I will say {D.he} did not hide anything.\""), .cross("Did you find food in the garage?", "\"Some food was there, old and dry. I would not call it a feeding setup.\""), .cross("How many animals survived?", "\"About forty-four. Some are still recovering.\""), .cross("Were the enclosures clean?", "\"They were crowded and in poor shape. I do not claim it was filthy beyond what neglect explains.\"")],
        defenseRole: "Landlord",
        defenseExam: [.direct("When did the power to the garage stop?", "\"Three weeks before the officers arrived. It was cut for an unpaid bill.\""), .direct("Did you hear from {D} during that time?", "\"Not once. {D} never called or came by about the power or the animals.\""), .direct("How did you learn of the smell?", "\"A tenant next door complained, so I opened the garage and saw what was inside.\""), .direct("What condition did you find the garage in?", "\"Cold, damp, and quiet. It was clear no one had been caring for the place.\""), .direct("Did you try to reach the defendant?", "\"Several times by phone. It went to voicemail, and I left messages about the smell.\""), .direct("What did you do when you saw the animals?", "\"I called the humane officers right away, because I knew it was serious.\""), .cross("Did you check on the garage during the three weeks?", "\"No. I did not go in. I assumed the rent was being paid and the place was fine.\""), .cross("Did the defendant pay the rent on time otherwise?", "\"Mostly. I had no complaint until this.\""), .cross("Was the defendant out of town, to your knowledge?", "\"I heard later about a medical stay. I did not know at the time.\""), .cross("Did the defendant ever give you notice about the animals?", "\"No. The lease did not mention them, and {DF} did not tell me.\""), .cross("Would a landlord notice a smell sooner?", "\"Probably. I should have checked sooner.\"")],
        theory: ("{D} left animals to die in a cold garage.", "A power failure."),
        allocution: "\"I could not keep up.\"",
        truths: ("{DL} bought two new animals after the power was cut.", "{DL} was out of town for a medical stay."),
        defendant: [.direct("Why did you keep about 70 snakes and lizards in a rented garage?", "\"I breed and keep reptiles. It was a growing hobby that became a small operation, and the garage was my space for it.\""), .direct("How did you care for them day to day?", "\"I fed, watered, and heated them with lamps and timers. I kept notes on feeding and shedding for each enclosure.\""), .direct("What happened when the power was cut?", "\"The lamps went dead, and the garage chilled. I did not realize how bad it would get so quickly.\""), .direct("Where were you during those weeks?", "\"I was out of town for a medical stay. I arranged for no one to cover, and I regret that.\""), .direct("What did you do when you learned?", "\"I rushed back and tried to understand. It was the worst thing I have seen.\""), .direct("What do you say to the animals' loss?", "\"I am heartbroken. I loved them, and I failed them.\""), .cross("You let the power bill go unpaid, didn't you?", "\"Yes. Money was tight, and I fell behind. I should have asked for help.\""), .cross("The water bowls were dry, weren't they?", "\"Yes. They were. I had no one to fill them.\""), .cross("You bought two new animals after the power was cut, didn't you?", "\"I did. That was a bad decision, and I made it before I understood how bad things were.\""), .cross("You never called your landlord, did you?", "\"No. I did not. I was in the hospital and ashamed.\""), .cross("Twenty-six animals died. Whose responsibility was that?", "\"Mine. I took them in, and I did not make sure they were cared for.\"")],
        openings: ("A landlord's complaint of a smell led officers to a rented garage where {D} kept about 70 snakes and lizards. Twenty-six were dead of cold and thirst, the rest dehydrated, with dry bowls and dead lamps after the power had been cut for weeks.", "{D} was an animal keeper who loved these reptiles, then went to a medical stay without cover while the power bill went unpaid. A failed plan, not a plan to hurt."),
        closings: ("Dry bowls, dead lamps, unpaid power, and twenty-six dead animals. A person who takes in seventy creatures answers for them, whether at home or in the hospital.", "The heat lamps died, a medical stay took {D} away, and no one was left to fill a bowl. That is sorrow and poor planning, not cruelty."),
        timeline: [(-21, "The power is cut."), (-10, "{DL} enters the hospital."), (0, "The landlord calls."), (12, "Charges.")],
        identified: "A landlord's complaint.",
        mood: .sympathetic,
        doctrines: ["burdenOfProof"])

    static let brotherNameForTwentyYearsV1 = SmallCases.make(
        key: "story.brotherNameForTwentyYears",
        category: .whiteCollar,
        headlines: ["Retiree's Pension Claim Unmasks a Man Living as His Dead Sibling", "Fingerprint Card Does Not Match the Name"],
        law: "identityTheft",
